WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.510
<i>The first time we met,</i>

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.020
<i>I saw a very thin boy standing before me.</i>

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.770
<i>After screaming at me not 
to come near or touch him,</i>

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.770
<i>he didn't speak another word.</i>

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:14.640
<i>He wouldn't even look at me.</i>

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.800
<i>There was nothing lovable about 
his perpetually expressionless face.</i>

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.720
<i>But his gaze seemed to gaze 
into a person's depths.</i>

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.930
<i>Honestly, it made me really uncomfortable.</i>

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.670
Ren, it's morning. Wake up.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.980
<i>But in reality, now that I've seen 
past his shell, I'm obsessed with him.</i>

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.930
<i>Even my excuse that I can't ignore him</i>

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.430
<i>because he's a child is wearing thin.</i>

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.690
Brother, don't you need 
to go pick up Haruko-san?

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.690
Nah. It's not her first time in Japan.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.270
I could go meet her.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:58.090
No, you have school and I have work.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.860
If your mom's coming here,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.700
maybe I'll stay at the 
Sagami house for a while.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:02.950
Aki?

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.110
I've never met her before, 
but honestly, I don't like her.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.960
She never even came to see him 
when he was in the hospital.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.460
But that was because...

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.470
What's more important than your dying son?

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.320
Ren, it's already 7:30. 
You're going to be late.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.010
I know.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.020
Haru, if you hear from Haruko, call me. 
Or you can e-mail me.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.480
Got it.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.500
International Airport

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.120
<i>Then, even though it was summer,</i>

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.440
<i>a storm named Haruko-san arrived.</i>

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:13.250
Ren, why have you been fiddling 
with your phone all morning?

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.550
You're like a millennial.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:19.760
I am a millennial. I know how to use a cell phone.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.460
Are you e-mailing your brother?

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.810
I got an e-mail saying Shima's going to Narita.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.260
I wanted to go.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.130
Narita? Do you have someone coming to visit?

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:30.910
Haruko.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.020
Who the hell is Haruko?

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.520
Haruko is Haru's mother.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.180
Your brother's mom? She must be beautiful.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.280
Of course.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:40.950
Oh?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.230
And she's smart, too.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.140
Yeah?

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.450
When Haruko was my age,

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.540
she had already finished her doctoral degree.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.050
Can I come see her?

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.200
No. I won't let you.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.320
Why not?

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:53.960
There'll be less.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:54.790
Less of what?

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.710
Brother? Yeah, I'm in the arrival lounge now.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.970
Yeah. He showed me a photo, 
but it was an old one.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:08.210
If Haruko-san contacts you, 
can you have her call my cell phone?

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.020
Actually, never mind. I think I found her.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.950
Wow... Just like the picture.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:18.270
Excuse me. You're Haruko-san, right?

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:19.390
Who are you?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.350
I'm Kaidou Shima.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:25.030
Oh, here. Haru's on the line.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:26.580
Mom?

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.850
I told you to call me Haruko-san, you idiot!

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:29.720
Wha—

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.040
<i>She hung up!</i>

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.430
<i>It's been seven years, 
and that's how she treats her son!</i>

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:38.290
You're Shima, huh? Did you come 
all the way here to meet me?

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.350
Anyway, you've grown.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:45.050
I've only seen photos of you when you 
were little, but I didn't recognize you.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.640
Are you sure you should have hung up on him?

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.630
Don't worry about it. 
Anyway, want to get some sushi?

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:56.060
<i>I think I understand why Ren likes her...</i>

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.520
What? Your mom is coming?

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.870
Didn't you say she was working overseas?

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.300
Is she coming back to Japan for work?

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.070
Gulp

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.070
Huh?

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.380
Oh... I'm not sure...

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:09.830
<i>And that's the question.</i>

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.830
<i>Why'd she come all the way from Switzerland</i>

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.560
You should've told me sooner.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.440
I need to mentally prepare myself.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.630
<i>when she's so busy, after 
just one e-mail from Ren?</i>

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.990
But maybe...

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.220
Does this mean you're in heat?

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:29.970
If it's not just Ren, but you, too,

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:32.350
then I'll have to re-discipline you.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:33.940
Welcome.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.040
Whoa, she's beautiful!

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.100
And young!

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.090
<i>Does she... know?!</i>

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:42.980
Haruko!

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:44.440
You're already here?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.620
I got here a while ago.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.320
Haru!

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.870
She got here before 
I could let you know. Sorry.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.520
You seem well. That's great.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.500
So do you.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.120
How long are you staying in Japan? 
I want to show you Tanuki.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.990
It looks like a dog to me.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.840
I feel like his owner has arrived.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.520
His name is Tanuki.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.840
You're not wrong.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.840
I see.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.040
Let me get a good look at your face.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.550
I thought you'd be small forever,

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:11.390
but you've grown a lot while 
I haven't been around.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.390
Your voice has changed, too. 
And you talk a lot now.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.100
Was I talking too much?

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:22.270
You dork. Nobody said that at all.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:25.820
I like your voice. Talk more.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.820
That's it!

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:27.860
What's wrong, Shima?

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.910
Oh... Nothing.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:34.510
<i>I knew our brother was a natural airhead...</i>

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.400
<i>I guess it's hereditary.</i>

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.150
<i>Ren has turned into a cat.</i>

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:44.670
Ren, go get changed and wash your hands. 
It's almost time for dinner.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.060
Okay.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.850
Well, I'm going to rest at a hotel for today.

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:52.760
Ren, I'll hear all of your stories later.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.480
A hotel? You're not staying here?

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.810
Yeah, right. I also came to 
Japan to work, you know.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.150
Disappointment

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:01.920
Oh...

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:09.130
Well, you know, Ren... I'm sure 
Haruko-san is busy with work.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.510
Excuse me, Haruko-san...

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:14.850
Aki's going to be staying with 
our grandparents for a while,

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:18.450
and I'll hardly be at home 
because of school and work.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:22.960
And since Haru's busy with the café, too, 
I think Ren has been lonely lately.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:24.580
So what?

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.960
If you don't mind our squalid household of men,

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.960
would you be willing to say here?

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.780
Oh, lord...

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:30.870
Right, Ren?

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.470
Yeah.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.850
Fine. I'll cancel my hotel reservation.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:38.970
<i>Sheesh...</i>

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.480
<i>Someone's been teaching him to 
act like a baby while I've been gone.</i>

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.980
Should we have Haruko-san 
stay in the Japanese-style room?

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.450
She can use my room. 
I don't use it much, anyway.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:55.450
You don't use it? 
Where on earth do you sleep?

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.560
Over there in Haru's room.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.500
I see...

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.750
It looks like I will have to re-discipline you.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.500
Y-You've got it all wrong!

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:09.080
Haru's bed is big, and I don't 
move much in my sleep.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.110
Ren, shut up for a second!

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:12.010
Sit!

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.260
This isn't self-destruction. 
It's... friendly fire?

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.770
I was worried since you 
sent me a weird e-mail,

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:23.810
but there's no way Haru 
wouldn't notice if you were sick.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:24.730
That was...

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.770
Were you able to resolve it?

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:30.280
Yeah. Sorry for making you worry.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.860
Don't worry about it. It's been 
a year and a half since I saw you.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.280
I wanted to see you again.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.030
Haru's memory seems to have returned, too.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:43.120
This reminds me of the summer seven 
years ago, when you were both at home.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:49.550
If that's what you think, I don't think anything 
has changed between me and Haru.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:53.570
In Haru's mind, I'm still that little boy.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.380
You don't want to be treated like a child?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.050
I don't know.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.730
Haru is quick to baby me,

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:03.840
but he says it's normal.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:06.060
Then there's nothing to worry about.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.880
He seems to be babying you, but he's 
actually being dependent on you.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:16.240
Surely you've noticed by now 
that Haru likes to do that.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.780
But why hasn't he said anything to you, then?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.220
Haru prefers you, both to depend on 
and to be depended on.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:34.050
Ren, it's late. I'm about to go to bed.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.950
You were talking for quite a while.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.410
I guess you and Haruko-san are close.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:43.790
There's something I find strange.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:49.800
You and Haruko are mother and son, 
but you hardly see each other or talk.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:53.620
It's not as if you don't get along, 
though, or that you don't care.

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:54.440
Huh?

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:59.000
Isn't this how most grown 
men and their mothers are?

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.600
As long as you know the other 
is doing well, it's fine.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.200
Really?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.550
There's no such thing as a child 
who doesn't like their own parents.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:13.480
When she suddenly told me 
to leave Canada for Japan,

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.840
I was mad that she'd made 
the decision for me.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:19.660
But now I know she did it for my sake...

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:21.800
What's wrong?

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.220
I'm going to sleep.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:27.580
Oh, so after I waited up for you, 
you don't want to talk to me?

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:30.640
<i>These moments make me feel like Haru 
and I are different in every way.</i>

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:35.110
<i>If what Haru says is true, 
then what am I doing here?</i>

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.950
Goodnight, Ren. It's great that 
Haruko-san came to visit, huh?

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.760
Was I acting that excited?

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:47.500
It's been like you couldn't even see me lately.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.550
Sorry.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.640
<i>After all, I don't have anything.</i>

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:54.420
<i>I guess my name means "zero" for a reason.</i>

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.260
Hey, welcome home.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:04.560
Aki, I thought you weren't 
coming home for a while.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:08.480
What? It's my house. 
I can come home anytime I want.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.440
It's almost Brother's birthday.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:16.270
He's probably forgotten, but we were 
talking about doing something for him.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:19.700
He's always such a pain in the ass.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.440
That's not a problem.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:24.450
Huh? You've already decided on something?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.700
What is it?

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:30.590
Haruko said everything Haru does for me 
is something he wants done for him.

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.740
Everything he does for you?

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:34.210
We can just do those things for him.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.420
Searching past...

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:41.510
I can't do that! I can't kiss my brother!

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:42.750
Aki, calm down.

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.930
I was just answering your question. 
Why are you acting like that?

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:47.930
By the way, what'd you do last year?

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.940
I made dinner. It was just curry, though.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.440
Ren's cooking...

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.980
I bet he really enjoyed that.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.690
Yeah. Since then, he's said...

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.990
Your curry is the best.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:02.600
...and hasn't made it again.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:05.200
No wonder he never makes us any.

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:07.370
That's good enough for me.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.430
Let's throw a curry party for his birthday.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:12.640
You just want to eat it yourself.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:13.360
Ren.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:14.650
What?

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:17.210
Mikiko-san's at the house.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:18.330
Mikiko?

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:22.630
She must be here to see Haruko-san. 
Could you get some tea for them?

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:23.980
Okay.

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.600
I looked into that matter for you.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:32.010
Finding people overseas 
isn't my specialty, you know.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:34.600
I'll pay. And?

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:36.500
The body you were looking for

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:40.610
was processed as unidentified 
ten years ago in Seattle.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.110
An Asian woman in her twenties.

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:46.920
Transported by ambulance from 
a motel in the outskirts of Seattle.

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.690
Died three days later of a drug overdose.

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:51.780
No ID on her.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:54.620
Not on the missing persons list, either.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.630
What about her case interests you?

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:01.160
I met a newspaper reporter 
while working in Seattle.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:05.640
His wife was Japanese and had been working 
as a nurse until a few years earlier.

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.390
She had a curious patient.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.390
A patient? You mean...

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.110
Before the woman died,

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:16.150
she said in Japanese that 
she sold her child to buy drugs.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:19.150
Oh, no... You don't mean her "child" is...

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.900
The child's name was "Ren" or "Allen."

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:25.550
She spoke with the police,

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:29.240
but there were no signs that a child 
had been living in the motel with her,

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.500
and nobody had seen one.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:33.910
But they'd always wondered about it.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.210
For crying out loud... 
Where and when was Ren found?

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:41.480
In a small town thirty 
kilometers east of Vancouver,

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:43.670
three months after the woman died.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.070
That's close.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:48.680
Are you going to tell him about this?

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:53.140
No. I wanted him to at least 
know his own background,

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:57.190
but there's no proof, 
and it's hardly a pleasant story.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:01.440
Besides, Ren never talks about what 
happened before he was taken in.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:05.990
If he doesn't want to remember, that's fine. 
If he's forgotten, that's even better.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.370
He already has a family.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.650
The boy living here is "Kaidou Ren."

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:18.020
<i>I have hardly any memories from 
before the orphanage took me in.</i>

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:23.090
<i>Aside from my name and birthday, 
there weren't any questions I could answer.</i>

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:27.570
<i>All I knew was that I was an unwanted child.</i>

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:33.240
<i>Of everyone I'd ever met, 
Haru was the most persistent.</i>

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:37.140
<i>So I hit, kicked,</i>

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.940
<i>scratched, and bit.</i>

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:45.930
<i>I didn't understand why he 
acted that way toward me.</i>

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:50.160
<i>It creeped me out. 
Kind people frightened me...</i>

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:53.160
Ren, what's wrong?

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:55.660
Was Haruko-san not there?

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.670
No, she was. They were talking about work.

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:02.680
I see. You wouldn't want to bother them, then.

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:07.420
Ren, seriously, what's wrong?

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:16.680
Ren, where's this service coming from?

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:18.380
Whoa...

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:21.980
Right here? What's gotten into you?

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.170
Nothing. If you don't want to, that's fine.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:26.440
Hey, wait!

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.780
Aw, jeez! Come with me!

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.060
Nobody will be coming here for a while.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.530
Haru, what about the café?

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.810
Aki and Shima are here today. 
They'll handle the rest.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.040
I see.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:41.700
<i>Is he regressing to his childhood?</i>

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:45.040
Fine, fine. Do what you want.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.940
<i>Since the day he learned 
Haruko-san was coming to Japan,</i>

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:53.300
<i>it's felt like someone hit 
the reset button on him.</i>

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:54.680
Haru...

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:59.310
Do I not have parents 
because I'm a bad child?

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.490
Huh? What are you—

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:04.940
I've always wondered.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.070
It's not that I wanted my own parents.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.860
I would rather have you instead.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:16.080
But do I have these strange feelings 
for you because I don't have parents?

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.750
The Kaidous took me in

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:23.060
to be your younger brother, right?

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:27.840
Aki and Shima live with me 
like it's totally natural.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:31.990
And Haruko, too... They accept me as "Kaidou Ren."

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:32.770
Ren?

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.840
But I don't care about that!

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:37.930
I'm here because

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:41.650
I can only be by your side as "Kaidou Ren"!

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:42.490
Ren...

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:47.280
Okay, I get it. I understand.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:52.910
Did Haruko-san and Mikiko-san 
say something about you?

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.370
If you don't want to tell me, 
you don't have to.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:59.400
Is it my fault?

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:03.370
Is it because yesterday I said there's no such 
thing as a child who hates their own parents?

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:04.570
No—

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.230
Sorry, Ren.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:10.240
You were taken from your parents before 
you were old enough to understand.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:14.150
You didn't understand what it meant 
to love or hate or be abandoned, right?

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:17.610
I don't care which family you're a part of.

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:19.120
Even if you're not a Kaidou,

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:24.080
as long as you're still the serious 
and stubborn Ren who loves me,

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.100
I don't care whose kid you are.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:31.650
The character in my name 
was given to me by Haruko.

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:34.330
Doesn't "rei" mean zero?

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:37.410
I thought it was perfect 
for me since I had nothing.

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.160
Zero?

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:42.410
Come to think of it, 
Haruko-san named me, too.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:46.630
Things had already fallen apart between 
her and my dad when I was born.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.320
She couldn't be bothered anymore,

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:57.180
What? Cooking? 
Laundry? Housework?

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:57.180
I'm not lifting a single 
finger to do any of that.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:52.810
so she named me "Haru" just like herself.

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:56.250
Maybe it was supposed to be 
a way to get revenge, too.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.180
Revenge?

00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:00.160
Every time my father called my name,

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.770
he'd be reminded of the woman he left.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.460
I don't get it.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:05.430
Why not?

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:08.760
Because your face is just like Haruko's.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.670
Even if he didn't say your name, 
he'd remember her every time he saw you.

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:17.450
Every time I saw Haruko's face, 
I remembered you.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.350
Ren! You're seriously so cute!

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:25.910
Squeeze

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:25.910
To thank you, I'll tell you something special.

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:29.950
Your name doesn't mean zero.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:31.670
Then what does it mean?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:36.490
The character "rei" in Japanese 
means "really small."

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.170
Rei

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.550
Sounds like something she'd do, right?

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:41.180
You really were sma—

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.680
Haruko!

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.410
What? I'm not an old woman.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.430
You don't have to shout. I can hear you.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.060
My name...

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.570
Your name? More importantly, we need to talk.

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:57.260
I wasn't going to tell you,

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:00.570
but I'm partly responsible, too.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.340
<i>Are you going to tell him about this?</i>

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:09.080
"April 1. I took in Tanuki."

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:12.190
"Haru says Tanuki isn't a raccoon dog,

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:15.340
so I went to see the raccoon 
dogs at the nearby zoo."

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:19.090
"Tanuki is not a raccoon dog. 
Tanuki is Tanuki."

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:21.180
What's the deal with Tanuki?

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.350
Oh, my. Is that Ren's essay?

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:26.970
You're too stupid. 
I have no idea what you're saying.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.650
Don't go through my things!

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:35.410
I thought a boy your age would have 
dirty magazines under his bed.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.960
Why were you hiding that, Ren?

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:39.440
I can do what I want!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:43.000
Mikiko told me you're having 
problems with modern Japanese.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:43.090
Souryou Academy 
Board Member

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.450
You have no trouble reading or listening,

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.620
but when it comes to speaking and writing, 
you're worse than a grade school student.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.940
It's not that bad...

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:53.600
That's right. You're exceptional in other areas.

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.550
Shut up, idiot.

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:58.900
Ren, unlike your brother 
behind you, you're smart.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:19:59.630
So mean!

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.640
All the people who have taught you before now

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.620
have been exceptional scholars 
with doctoral degrees.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.360
Yet, apparently, your special lectures

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:11.140
were suspended over a single essay.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.900
M-My homeroom teacher said I lack emotion...

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:19.880
I've been letting it slide since you 
said you wanted to live with Haru,

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.400
Harvard Graduate

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.400
IQ 185

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.400
Current CERN Researcher

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.400
but this affects my pride.

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.910
Wait, what are you talking about?

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:27.760
It's never too late to start over.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:31.410
Fortunately, there are plenty of prestigious 
schools in Switzerland, as well.

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:36.370
The people who've taught you since you 
were little are members of CERN, too.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:39.930
The world's most exceptional 
physicists gather there.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:41.940
There's no better environment for you.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:46.180
I'm taking you back to Switzerland with me.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.420
What?!

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:50.930
You got a problem with that?

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:55.110
<i>How did it suddenly come to this?</i>

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:28.800
A scream?

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:31.490
Bro's probably up to something stupid again.

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:35.500
Ow! She punched me as hard as she could...

00:22:35.930 --> 00:22:39.130
That's because you called 
Haruko a rotten old hag.

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:43.250
Yeah, because she suddenly announced 
that she's taking you to Switzerland!

00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:45.380
What are you talking about, 
you rotten old ha—

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:47.840
The rest omitted.

00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:51.320
Yeah, that was an impressive right straight.

00:22:52.110 --> 00:22:53.570
It's okay.

00:22:53.570 --> 00:22:57.770
I'm not going to Switzerland, 
and I'm not leaving you.

00:22:57.970 --> 00:22:58.850
Ren...

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:01.260
You're right.

00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:05.250
I can't imagine living without you.

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:08.030
If you left me, I'd die of loneliness.

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:12.300
Die of loneliness? 
Is your oldest son a rabbit?

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:14.280
Whatever.

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:16.690
I'll be staying a while longer.

00:23:16.690 --> 00:23:19.290
Ren, you and I will have a 
nice, long chat tomorrow.

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:20.520
Got it.

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:22.290
Got what?

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:24.830
<i>Out of the pan and into the fire...</i>

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:29.510
<i>I have a feeling the storm called 
Haruko-san is going to continue.</i>

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:30.140
To be continued...?
